{
  "schema_version": "report-evidence/1",
  "source_sha256": "d0c70d7fc6115abd543be4c6713df6e873edd4089f9ec9fa15a9c7974c8bf930",
  "fragments": [
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0001",
      "text": "# Incorrect tuple destructuring in RiskEngine.twapEMA produces wrong TWAP",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 73,
      "line": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0002",
      "text": "- Severity: High",
      "start": 74,
      "end": 90,
      "line": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0003",
      "text": "## Targets",
      "start": 92,
      "end": 102,
      "line": 4
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0004",
      "text": "- `RiskEngine.twapEMA`",
      "start": 103,
      "end": 125,
      "line": 5
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0005",
      "text": "- `OraclePack.getEMAs`",
      "start": 126,
      "end": 148,
      "line": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0006",
      "text": "## Summary",
      "start": 150,
      "end": 160,
      "line": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0007",
      "text": "`RiskEngine.twapEMA` destructures the tuple returned by `oraclePack.getEMAs()` in the wrong order. `getEMAs()` returns `(spotEMA, fastEMA, slowEMA, eonsEMA, medianTick)`, but `twapEMA` binds the first three values as `(eonsEMA, slowEMA, fastEMA, , )`. This swaps the EMA components and drops the real eons EMA, producing an incorrect time-weighted price signal.",
      "start": 162,
      "end": 523,
      "line": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0008",
      "text": "## Vulnerability details",
      "start": 525,
      "end": 549,
      "line": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0009",
      "text": "`OraclePack.getEMAs()` returns (in-order):",
      "start": 551,
      "end": 593,
      "line": 14
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0010",
      "text": "- `spotEMA`",
      "start": 594,
      "end": 605,
      "line": 15
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0011",
      "text": "- `fastEMA`",
      "start": 606,
      "end": 617,
      "line": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0012",
      "text": "- `slowEMA`",
      "start": 618,
      "end": 629,
      "line": 17
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0013",
      "text": "- `eonsEMA`",
      "start": 630,
      "end": 641,
      "line": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0014",
      "text": "- `medianTick`",
      "start": 642,
      "end": 656,
      "line": 19
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0015",
      "text": "But `twapEMA` does:",
      "start": 658,
      "end": 677,
      "line": 21
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0016",
      "text": "- `eonsEMA <- spotEMA`",
      "start": 678,
      "end": 700,
      "line": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0017",
      "text": "- `slowEMA <- fastEMA`",
      "start": 701,
      "end": 723,
      "line": 23
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0018",
      "text": "- `fastEMA <- slowEMA`",
      "start": 724,
      "end": 746,
      "line": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0019",
      "text": "- (drops the real `eonsEMA`)",
      "start": 747,
      "end": 775,
      "line": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0020",
      "text": "The returned blended tick is therefore effectively computed from the wrong inputs.",
      "start": 777,
      "end": 859,
      "line": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0021",
      "text": "## Code references (original)",
      "start": 861,
      "end": 890,
      "line": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0022",
      "text": "- Wrong destructuring in `twapEMA`: [contracts/RiskEngine.sol](../contracts/RiskEngine.sol#L836-L841)",
      "start": 892,
      "end": 993,
      "line": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0023",
      "text": "- Correct return order in `getEMAs`: [contracts/types/OraclePack.sol](../contracts/types/OraclePack.sol#L210-L223)",
      "start": 994,
      "end": 1108,
      "line": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0024",
      "text": "## Root cause",
      "start": 1110,
      "end": 1123,
      "line": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0025",
      "text": "Fragile positional tuple destructuring: the caller assumes a different return order than the callee.",
      "start": 1125,
      "end": 1225,
      "line": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0026",
      "text": "## Impact",
      "start": 1227,
      "end": 1236,
      "line": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "e_d0c70d7fc611_0027",
      "text": "High — `twapEMA` returns an incorrect price signal. Any downstream component using this TWAP for pricing, risk, margin, safe-mode gating, or liquidation decisions can be distorted. This can lead to mispriced risk, wrongful liquidations, missed liquidations, or systemic solvency issues.",
      "start": 1238,
      "end": 1524,
      "line": 40
    }
  ]
}
